summary: 'Probe P02 proved a Passport-KSP P-256 key with NgcCacheType AUTH_MANDATORY prompts on every use; the founder answered the prompts. The helper gained a separate Hello presence key: on fresh decisions it signs the presence challenge under a Hello prompt owned by the foreground window, while the approvals key signs the decision. The kernel verifies presence only against the Hello keyId, and the dev binding gains a root-signed presence row. Verified live: an always rule took one PIN. Aegis ship-with-fixes folded in: the AUTH_MANDATORY read-back, root class refused, keyId/PEM checks, and an orphan-key hint. The GUI approve timeout was raised to 150 s.'
